   "tutor": "Here is the rule: for a finished past action, add -ed to most verbs: walk - walked, move - moved, carry - carried.\nRight: \"On Monday the farmer counted the sheep.\" Wrong: \"On Monday the farmer count the sheep.\" The action is finished, so the plain verb without -ed does not fit.\nLet me think aloud with one example: \"Last week the puppy carried a stick.\" Step 1: last week shows a finished time. Step 2: carry ends in a consonant plus y, so y becomes i. Step 3: I add -ed.\nNow your turn. Check the time word, then write one word:\nWrite the past form: On Saturday the children ___ (kick) the ball in the park.",
